# Smart Factory OEE — Performance Monitoring & Optimisation (Data Engineering–Led)

An end-to-end manufacturing analytics pipeline built in Python to ingest, validate, clean, and model OEE and downtime data using a layered Bronze → Silver → Gold architecture. The output is analytics-ready KPI and optimisation tables designed for consumption in Power BI or other BI tools.

This project demonstrates data engineering best practices including data quality validation, reproducible transformations, and separation of raw and derived data layers.

---

## Data

Synthetic OEE and downtime CSV exports stored in `data/bronze/`:

- `oee_by_day.csv` — daily machine OEE metrics  
- `oee_by_shift.csv` — shift-level OEE metrics  
- `downtime_pareto.csv` — downtime causes and durations

These datasets simulate production exports from a manufacturing execution or historian system.

---

## Pipeline Architecture

The pipeline follows a standard layered data architecture:

### Bronze — Raw Ingestion
- Raw CSVs as received from the source system
- No modification except schema validation and quality checks

### Silver — Cleaned & Standardised
- Type casting and schema enforcement
- Null, duplicate, and value range validation
- Column standardisation and basic transformations

### Gold — Analytics & Optimisation Outputs
- KPI summary tables
- Worst-performing shift analysis
- Pareto analysis of top downtime causes
- Recommended optimisation action table

Gold outputs are written to `data/gold/` and are not version-controlled.

